---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Notice from "../components/Notice.astro";
import { site } from "../config";

const description = `Privacy policy for ${site.name}, published by ${site.publisher}. The game stores progress on your device and does not create an account.`;
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={description}>
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="kicker">Privacy Policy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {site.updated}</p>
    <Notice />

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} does not ask you to create an account. Your progress stays on your device. We do
      not receive that save, and we do not sell personal information. When advertising is turned on,
      Google AdMob may receive an advertising identifier to show ads. Purchases are handled by Apple
      or Google.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {site.publisher} publishes {site.name} for iOS and Android. The app id on both stores is
      <span>{site.bundleId}</span>. Privacy questions go to
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app does not collect</h2>
    <p>
      The app does not ask for your name, email address, phone number, contacts, photos, precise
      location, or microphone. It does not create an account. It does not add its own encryption
      beyond what the phone already provides. The iOS build declares that it does not use
      non-exempt encryption.
    </p>
    <p>
      On Android, the app may use permission to change audio settings so game sound can follow the
      game's own volume. It does not record audio.
    </p>

    <h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      The game stores your progress on the phone or tablet. That includes levels you have reached,
      scores, energy, shards, cosmetics you have unlocked, settings, and related game state. The
      on-device save is named {site.saveKey}. It is not uploaded to us.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you delete the app, or clear the app's storage, that save is deleted with it. We cannot
      restore it, because we never received a copy. The steps are on the
      <a href="/data">Your Data</a> page.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Store builds may show ads through Google AdMob. AdMob can receive an advertising identifier,
      basic device and app information, and information about an ad that was shown or tapped. Google
      handles that data under its own policy at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      How ads appear is in the <a href="/advertising">Advertising Policy</a>. Rewarded ads are
      optional. Interstitial ads run between attempts, not while you are aiming and not while Spark
      is in flight.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can limit how ads use an identifier in your device settings. On iPhone, you can refuse a
      tracking request if one appears, turn off Allow Apps to Request to Track, and reset the
      advertising identifier. On Android, you can delete the advertising ID or opt out of ads
      personalization. Ads can still appear.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you buy Remove Ads, forced interstitial ads stop. You can still choose to watch a rewarded
      ad.
    </p>

    <h2>Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Energy, shards, cosmetics, and Remove Ads are offered, when they are offered, through the
      Apple App Store or Google Play. Apple or Google processes the payment. We do not receive your
      card number or full payment account details. The store may tell the game, on your device,
      that a purchase succeeded so it can unlock what you bought.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The app does not send gameplay or diagnostic analytics to us. There is no remote analytics
      service in the app. If a future version adds crash reports or gameplay diagnostics, this
      policy will be updated before that version is released.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
      information from children. If you believe a child has emailed us personal information, write
      to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will delete that correspondence.
      The game does not give us an account or a profile to delete.
    </p>

    <h2>Selling personal information</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it with data brokers. Advertising,
      when it is enabled, is served by Google as described above. If you are a California resident,
      you can email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with a privacy request. In
      the ordinary case, the only information we hold is an email you chose to send.
    </p>

    <h2>Email you send us</h2>
    <p>
      If you email {site.email}, we use that message to answer you and keep the correspondence in
      our email account. You can ask us to delete it. We do not use it as a marketing list.
    </p>

    <h2>Other companies</h2>
    <p>
      Apple, Google Play, and Google AdMob may process purchase and advertising data in the
      countries where they operate, under their own terms. We do not run a server that receives
      your game save.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the date at the top will change and the new version will be posted on
      this page. A change that affects advertising or analytics will be posted here before the
      matching app version is released.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {site.publisher}<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
